## Verdict

fail: 1 Blocker (F1), 2 Major (F2, F3), 1 Nit (F4). retry_recommendation: escalate_human.

## Paraphrase

### What this track proposes

The addendum makes one app package for each of weeks 2 to 7. It runs the Phase 7 book-picture script on 6 weeks and writes 108 JPEGs and 6 provenance files. It writes 18 image.file lines into each week file and keeps every approval draft. It adds one test on a temporary copy of a week and drops image.file in the loops-content compare. It sends 6 hand-off folders to the PM by 2026-11-16 and puts the owner items on the 11-16 list.

### How the current system works, per this spec

Weeks 2 to 7 are draft packages. Their text and Thai approvals are approved; the images, audio, song, scripts and loops approvals are draft. No book cover or page of these weeks names a picture. The Phase 7 script matches pictures.json rows by week, use and text, resolves the COLOR file through the Forge manifest, writes 1600 px JPEGs and a provenance file, and adds image.file lines. The book-pictures check reads those paths. Week 1 is published and its 18 pictures are set.

## Findings

- F1 [Blocker] Addendum 2026-11-05 Overview and FR 1: the claim that the Phase 7 script "works for any week, because it matches the rows by week.meta.week" is false for w02 and w06. Rationale: w02 decodable pages 1 to 6 repeat "Nan can.", "Can I?" and "I can!"; w06 decodable pages 3 and 6 both say "Tap, tap, tap!"; pictures.json holds a second week 2 row for each of the three texts (nan-can-b, can-i-b, i-can-b) and a second week 6 row (tap-tap-tap-b); set-book-pictures.ts line 51 filters by week, use and text, so each repeated page gets 2 candidates and line 52 exits 1 before any write; E2 and D3 forbid a change to the match, and the addendum gives no rule for which row to take and no rule for the file to change; the fallback "unless a defect shows; the maker reports it then" names no decision.
- F2 [Major] FR 6 and E7: the new test names no file path, no week and no assertion. Rationale: the blast radius says "the new test file of E7" but gives no path, and the RED and GREEN commands name only the existing storytime-book-pictures.test.ts and storytime-loops-content.test.ts; the existing test already covers the failure modes on temporary copies and the success case on the shipped w01; the maker must guess the file name, the week, and the checks.
- F3 [Major] E5 and E3: the order between the 11-16 hand-off and the later approval.images edit is not defined. Rationale: E5 requires the week file to be byte-equal to a commit and one line to the PM; E3 puts the words edit in a later task; the addendum does not say which commit the folder takes or whether a second folder follows the edit.
- F4 [Nit] Blast radius: "Any test that counts the check rows of weeks 2 to 7 changes too. The maker greps for them and lists them." leaves the changed test set to a grep and names no test. Rationale: other tests read every week, so the maker must find the set and the pattern.

## Zero-decision check: places where the maker must guess

1. Which row to take for w02 pages 1, 2, 3 and 4, 5, 6, and for w06 pages 3 and 6 (F1); and which file to change to remove the ambiguity.
2. The file path, week and assertions of the E7 test (F2).
3. Which commit the hand-off week file takes, and whether a second folder or PM line follows the approval edit (F3).
4. The changed test set for weeks 2 to 7 (F4).

## Zoom-out check

The addendum solves the root problem (the app has no pictures for weeks 2 to 7). It adds no speculative feature and no premature optimization. It reuses set-book-pictures.ts, checkBookPictures and resolveStorytimePictureFiles. It puts the work in the Phase 7 place. It stays at the requirement level, except the test detail of F2. It meets the PM order: one package per week, the same contract and checks as week 1, Daniel items on the 11-16 list, not a stop.

## Facts checked

- HEAD equals audited_head_sha.
- Covers, pages and audio: 6 weeks, 2 books x (1 cover + 8 pages); each book has audio.file and slowFile.
- Cover rows and story-page rows: exactly one for every cover and for 104 of the 108 pages; 4 pages (w02 p1 to p6 share 3 texts, w06 p3 and p6) have 2 rows each. No item has zero rows.
- No image.file on weeks 2 to 7; w01 has its 18.
- Approvals of weeks 2 to 7 match the addendum.
- The one accepted FAIL stays: only w01 is published and its approval.loops is draft.
- book-pictures check matches the addendum.
- E5 model folder w01 exists and matches the E5 form.
- Not verified: the v15 proof, the print approval of weeks 2 to 7, the media path counts of w03 to w07.

